ppearing and  fighting with my family whose production  he spearheaded what are your names good  my name it doesn't matter what your  names are you walk around here  interrupting the rock  like you haven't seen the Sun in 20  years you like to just stepped out of  Oliver Twist next year Johnson's got  Disney's Jungle Cruise and action comedy  red notice co-starring his DC EU  stablemate gal gadot he also stars on  HBO's ballers host a reality competition  he created called the Titan Games on NBC  and has quite a few films in various  stages of production plus he's active as  a producer on multiple movies he's  working on releasing a tequila and he's  helping design products for his project  rock collaboration with Under Armour  plus he's working out like a beast and  raising a family 2016 s People's Sexiest  Man Alive is busy with a capital B and  chances are good that he simply hasn't  had the time to work a Marvel movie into  his crazy schedule yet some actors just  looked tailor-made for their roles has  there ever been a more James Bond  looking James Bond than Pierce Brosnan  can you think of a more appropriate man  to play the mountain on Game of Thrones  than actual world Strongest Man Thor  Bernsen and when it comes to superheroes  who is more qualified to play one than  real-life superhuman to wane the rock  Johnson the rock has a physique that  looks like it was drawn by Rob Leah  fells so it seems like a no-brainer that  he should find himself a spot in the MCU  the only problem is Marvel prefers to go  with the unexpected when it comes to  their superhero casting when the studio  needed to cast star-lord the suave  leader of the guardians of the galaxy  they didn't go out and get Chris Pine or  James Marsden they went with Chris Pratt  who at the time was best known as a  somewhat schlubby sitcom actor they also  went with funny man Paul Rudd for  ant-man  relative unknowns Chris Hemsworth and  Tom Hiddleston for Thor and Loki  respectively and they cast the  supposedly washed-up over-the-hill and  problematic Robert Downey jr. as Iron  Man the guy who ended up leading the  entire franchise and although Marvel  sometimes does what's expected the  studio may think that casting the rock  as a superhero is a little too  on-the-nose for their brand as his level  of stardom has grown over the last  handful of years so has the rocks level  of influence in Hollywood seven bucks  Productions the studio Johnson founded  with his ex-wife Danny Garcia in 2012  has produced every single movie the  actor has starred in since 2017 s  Baywatch not only that but Johnson  wields a consid  durable amount of power over those films  he's very cautious about maintaining his  image and he's known to be pretty  inflexible when it comes to certain  aspects of his films for example he  forced a change to the ending of rampage  so the guerrilla wouldn't die at the end  plus he broke away from his role in The  Fast &amp; Furious franchise to lead his own  spin-off Hobbs and Shaw no one tells me  what to do Johnson has shown that he  likes to be in control of his films and  if there's one studio that's not known  for giving up control  it's Marvel with the exception of the  spider-man movies which are produced in  coordination with Sony Pictures since  they owned the film rights to the  character Marvel Studios doesn't share  production credit with any other studio  the Studios President Kevin Feige has  the final say on everything in the MCU  and Johnson may not be willing to cede  the control he's become accustomed to  just for a spot in a Marvel movie in  spite of all the factors working against  the rock joining the MCU it still seems  like there may be something going on  between them that we just don't know  about yet at the 2019 MTV Movie Awards  Avengers and Game Director Anthony Russo  joked that Johnson should join the MCU  as himself but the most compelling piece  of evidence comes in the form of a  throwaway line Johnson included 